-- title:
--   Residual modularity via maximal ideals of the Hecke algebra
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $\mathbb{Z}$, let $p$ and $M$ be natural numbers with $M \neq 0$, and assume the integral-structure hypothesis [`CuspForm.HasIntegralStructure M 2`](def/CuspForm_IntegralStructure.html#L6): the $\mathbb{C}$-span of [`CuspForm.intLattice M 2`](def/CuspForm_IntegralStructure.html#L3), the $\mathbb{Z}$-span of those weight-$2$ cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(M)$ all of whose $q$-expansion coefficients are rational integers, is the whole space. Write $S = \{\ell \mid (\ell : \mathbb{Z}) \mathrel{|} \Delta_W\} \cup \{p\} \cup \{\ell \mid \ell \mathrel{|} M\}$ and let $\mathbb{T} =$ [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra M 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) be the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}(S_2(\Gamma_0(M)))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid M$, $\ell \notin S$, together with the $U_q$ for primes $q \mid M$, $q \notin S$ (there are none, as $S$ contains all divisors of $M$). Then $W$ is residually modular of level $M$ at $p$ — i.e. there exist a weight-$2$ cusp form $f$ on $\Gamma_0(M)$ satisfying the normalised-eigenform conditions ($a_1(f) = 1$, multiplicativity of $a_n(f)$ in coprime indices, and the two prime-power recursions according to whether the prime divides $M$) and a maximal ideal $\mathfrak{M}$ of the ring $\overline{\mathbb{Z}}$ of algebraic integers in $\mathbb{C}$ with $p \in \mathfrak{M}$ and, for every prime $\ell$ with $(\ell : \mathbb{Z}) \nmid \Delta_W$, $\ell \nmid M$, $\ell \neq p$, an algebraic integer $a$ with $a = a_\ell(f)$ and $a - a_\ell(W) \in \mathfrak{M}$, where $a_\ell(W) = \ell + 1 - \#W(\mathbb{F}_\ell)$ for the reduction of $W$ modulo $\ell$ — if and only if $\mathbb{T}$ has a maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}$ containing $p$ and containing $T_\ell - a_\ell(W)$ for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid M$ and $\ell \notin S$. No primality hypothesis is imposed on $p$.
--
--   This is the dictionary between residual modularity of an elliptic curve at $p$, phrased through a normalised eigenform congruent to the trace-of-Frobenius system modulo a prime of $\overline{\mathbb{Z}}$, and the existence of a maximal ideal of the anemic Hecke algebra of level $M$ cutting out the same residual eigensystem. It is used both to extract a residual eigensystem from residual modularity and to establish residual modularity from a proper ideal of the Hecke algebra.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_isResiduallyModularOfLevel_iff_exists_ideal_heckeAlgebra.lean

